---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Accessibility"
  description="What AMDai tests for keyboard, screen-reader, and mobile access — and how to report a problem."
>
  <main id="main" class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <p class="kicker">Access</p>
    <h1 class="display mt-3 text-4xl sm:text-5xl">Accessibility</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
      AMDai is a public documentation site. Visitors use phones, keyboards, and screen readers.
      This page records what we test and how to tell us when something is in the way.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl">What we test</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-muted">
        <li>axe-core on every built page, in the default dark theme and the light theme. Serious and critical findings fail <code class="text-ink">npm run qa:a11y</code>.</li>
        <li>Keyboard: a skip-to-content link, a visible focus ring, Path / Tools / Learn menus (Enter, Space, Escape, arrow keys), and the calculator and Qwen compare filters without a mouse.</li>
        <li>Live-region announcements when calculator totals change.</li>
        <li>prefers-reduced-motion: decorative motion stops.</li>
        <li>Mobile widths 360, 390, and 768. Wide tables scroll in their own container. Inputs stay at 16px so iOS does not zoom.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl">Last pass</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Automated plus keyboard and mobile pass: <strong class="text-ink">13 October 2026</strong>.
        The dated axe report is written next to the site-wide link QA reports under
        <code class="text-ink">artifacts/link-reports/</code> and <code class="text-ink">reports/</code>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl">Report a problem</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Use the existing public routes — we do not publish a separate inbox on this page.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-muted">
        <li>
          <a class="underline decoration-accent/40 underline-offset-2" href="/forum">Forum</a>
          — threads when the forum is on; the
          <a class="underline decoration-accent/40 underline-offset-2" href="/forum/rules">code of conduct</a>
          still applies when it is off.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a class="underline decoration-accent/40 underline-offset-2" href="/contribute">Contribute</a>
          — recipe JSON and sourced notes. Say the page URL, the browser, and whether you were on a phone or a keyboard.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
